                        "quest": "a_record_is_not_the_thing",
                        "stage": "the_field_books"
                    }
                ],
                "text": "\"Rivermark,\" says the woman at the top of the ladder, and comes down it with a stack of narrow, swollen books bound in green cloth. \"Forty-one field books. Chain, angles, levels, the margins.\" She lays them on the long table. \"A penny a page to read, a penny to copy, and nothing leaves the room. You'll have brought a copy of your own. People do.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Lay the survey beside them.",
                        "next": "beside"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "conditions": [
                    {
                        "quest": "the_fenmoor_lot",
                        "stage": "lot_forty_one"
                    }
                ],
                "text": "\"The Fenmoor lot,\" Dorcas Fenn says from the ladder. \"Greyhythe returns, four years back.\" The ladder rolls along the rail, three yards, five, and stops. \"Here.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Read the return.",
