                    {
                        "flag": "fenmoor_no_name"
                    }
                ],
                "once": true,
                "text": "\"One in forty,\" Dorcas Fenn says, when you tell her about the margin. She thinks about it at the top of the ladder for some time. \"I've had clerks forget a name one time in four. I've had a clerk forget his own.\" The ladder rolls a yard. \"That's not me telling you it means nothing. It's me telling you this room can't tell you whether it does.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Anything?",
