        ],
        "the_quarry": [
            {
                "text": "Dorcas Fenn goes up the ladder and comes back down with one thin file and opens it. Two letters from Mr Corse, asking what the works at the head of the valley are for. Two replies, each a revised figure and a request for a fuller return. Nothing else. \"That's all there is,\" she says. \"If anybody knew, it'd be here. Somebody would have had to write it down.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Leave.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
        "fenmoor_return": [
            {
                "text": "She comes down with a thin bound book and opens it on the long table without looking for the page.\n\nLot 41. Sundry armour, the Fenmoor stock, the property of the house. To T. Vass, dealer in second goods, Greyhythe. 31 gp. Duty paid.\n\n\"Vass files as well,\" Dorcas Fenn says. \"Dealers must, for the duty, and he is a careful man, which is to say a frightened one.\" Another book, another page that she does not look for.\n\nPlate, three suits and pieces, as bought. To Brindle & Daughter, chandlers, Brackwater wharf. 40 gp.\n\n\"Tuppence,\" she says. \"Two pages.\"",
                "interjections": [
                    {
                        "companion": "sera",
                        "text": "Sera, reading upside down: \"Thirty-one, then forty. Everybody made nine gold off it and nobody made a decision.\""
                    },
                    {
                        "companion": "kessa",
                        "text": "Kessa: \"Brindle's. That's under the arches. I bought a knife there.\" A pause. \"Second-hand.\""
                    }
                ],
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Pay the tuppence. Brindle & Daughter, then.",
                        "conditions": [
                            {
                                "quest": "the_fenmoor_lot",
                                "stage": "lot_forty_one"
                            }
                        ],
                        "effects": [
                            {
                                "quest_stage": {
                                    "quest": "the_fenmoor_lot",
                                    "stage": "brindle_and_daughter"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
                        "end": true
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "Do people often come asking where a thing went?",
                        "next": "fenmoor_often"
                    },
                    {
                        "label": "Leave.",
                        "end": true
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
        "fenmoor_often": [
            {
                "text": "\"Every week,\" Dorcas Fenn says. \"Widows, mostly, and heirs, and once a man looking for a horse.\" She closes the book. \"They want the last page. There isn't a last page. There's only the page where it stopped being anybody's business to write it down.\"",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "label": "Brindle & Daughter, then.",
                        "conditions": [
                            {
                                "quest": "the_fenmoor_lot",
                                "stage": "lot_forty_one"
                            }
                        ],
                        "effects": [
                            {
                                "quest_stage": {
